WEBVTT



00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.980
Web testing is rarely one task.

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:03.660
Teams must design cases,

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:06.120
implement automation, run every path, collect

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:07.860
evidence, and explain the result.

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:10.960
That workflow consumes valuable engineering time.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:13.860
EagleEye changes the starting point.

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:15.740
Turn on the browser agent, use

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:16.620
the site normally,

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:18.200
and your real journey becomes the

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:19.300
seed for observation,

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:21.500
generation, replay, explanation,

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:22.220
and sharing.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:26.820
Here, the Chrome extension is explicitly

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:28.660
on while a real local Authorized target

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:30.140
site is used as usual.

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:31.620
When recording is off,

00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:33.080
EagleEye captures nothing.

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:34.660
When it is on, this session

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:36.100
produced four observations.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:44.960
EagleEye keeps only the context needed

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:46.200
for quality assurance,

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:48.300
a privacy-safe DOM summary,

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:49.400
the visible screenshot,

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:50.560
and the action trail.

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:52.400
Form values, passwords,

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:54.340
tokens, and other secret inputs are

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:55.060
not retained.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:02.720
GPT-5.6 through Codex App Server expands the recorded

00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:04.540
path with complementary tests.

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:06.900
The original case stays deterministic.

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:09.060
This run produced five cases, used

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:10.980
no fallback and passed quality review

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:11.660
at one hundred.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:15.980
Now press replay,

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:17.960
Playwright not the language model, executes

00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:19.540
the same journey and checks the

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:21.500
URL, title, and heading against the

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:22.820
real Authorized target page.

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:24.780
AI proposes coverage.

00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:27.040
The deterministic runner decides pass or

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:27.420
fail.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:38.300
This replay passed in 1,745 milliseconds.

00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:40.600
EagleEye preserved the screenshot,

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:42.420
WebM recording, byte counts,

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:45.580
timestamp, and SHA-256 receipts.

00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:47.240
A pass is not just a

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:49.220
message, it is verifiable evidence.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:55.420
EagleEye can also explain likely improvements

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:56.660
and suggest fixes,

00:01:57.060 --> 00:01:58.180
but applying code,

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:00.400
operating production and approving a release

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:01.720
remain human decisions.

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:03.960
The agent proposes people stay in

00:02:03.980 --> 00:02:04.480
control.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:07.040
Finally, intent recorded steps,

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:09.500
AI-generated cases, replay results,

00:02:09.620 --> 00:02:11.940
improvement suggestions, and evidence are assembled

00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:13.020
into one report.

00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:15.080
The same result can be exported

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:16.820
as a markdown bug report and

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:18.380
handed directly to engineering,

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:19.860
so the QA loop ends with

00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:21.340
an artifact the whole team can

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:21.800
use.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.920
Observe reality, generate coverage,

00:02:32.140 --> 00:02:34.400
replay proof. EagleEye is a browser-native

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:36.560
AI QA agent that watches approved

00:02:36.580 --> 00:02:38.900
journeys, expands them with OpenAI,

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:40.800
verifies them with Playwright, and delivers

00:02:40.820 --> 00:02:42.380
evidence your team can share,

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:44.640
less testing overhead without giving up

00:02:44.660 --> 00:02:45.200
control.
